    "created_at": "2025-07-10T12:04:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-10T12:04:11Z",
    "body": "> Indeed. We currently only use an [async iterable _declaration_](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-async-iterable-declaration), we don't (yet) use an [async iterable _type_](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-async-iterable-type).\n\nOops. That's quite a confusing distinction. 😅 \n\nFor context: I saw that spec change got merged, searched Ladybird's IDL files for \"async iterable\", and ReadableStream was the only result. My apologies if this is a false alarm!",
    "author_association": "NONE",
